# apricorn input v1
#
# The new-game corpus case: the retail ROM driven from power-on to the
# player's bedroom (map 64) with the field fade-in complete. The oracle
# boots with a blank card, so the title screen goes straight to the
# new-game flow (no main menu); the frame timings below were measured
# on the oracle with --shots and are documented in README.md.
rtc 2010-03-01T09:00:00
end 5000

# Intro movie (scene 1, skippable once its title card is up): A skips it.
1000 down A
1002 up A

# Title screen: A advances (never UP+SELECT+B, the save-clear combo).
1300 down A
1302 up A

# Oak's button tutorial prompt (three options): the first B enters pad
# mode, the second B picks the last entry, "no info needed".
1700 down B
1702 up B
1710 down B
1712 up B

# Oak's dialogs page-wait on a fresh A press, so A is pulsed (4 down, 4
# up) through the speech. The same pulses drive the gender pick (the
# first press arms the pad, the second confirms the resting cursor: the
# boy) and the gender confirmation's YES. They stop before the naming
# screen fades in (~3850): on the keyboard A would type the cursor's key.
